'''2215 Avinguda Embarcadero''' is a 57-storey luxury residential tower at 2215 [[Avinguda Embarcadero]] in the [[Molls Superiors (Original, Sant Cristòfor)|Molls Superiors]] barri of [[Original (ciutat)|Original]], [[Sant Cristòfor]], [[Balboa]]. Completed in 2015, the tower was developed by [[Grup Ciutat Nova]] and is the tallest residential building in Sant Cristòfor. At 205 metres (673 ft), it is also one of the tallest buildings in the city.

== Architecture ==

The tower is a slender residential skyscraper with a clean late-modern design and a distinctive sculptural crown. The main shaft is a tall rectangular slab clad in a pale beige, rose-grey, and lightly tinted stone-and-glass exterior. The façade is relatively restrained, using repetitive horizontal window bands and narrow vertical strips rather than a fully glazed curtain wall, giving the building a residential character distinct from the darker office towers of the nearby [[Districte Financer (Original, Sant Cristòfor)|Districte Financer]].

The most recognisable feature is the asymmetrical roof structure. One side of the crown rises into a sloping frame or blade-like canopy with open cut-outs beneath it, which conceals mechanical equipment while creating a strong silhouette on the Sant Cristòfor skyline. The crown may also contain a rooftop lounge, duplex penthouse levels, and private terraces below the canopy.

The tower is broad when viewed front-on but thin from the side, with a rectangular floor plate of approximately 950 to 1,100 m². The building is designed to catch the golden light at sunset, when the lighter façade and crown become especially prominent against the bay.

