=== Apartment arrangement ===

The lower floors contain the lobby, residents' club, fitness centre, spa, indoor pool, lounges, and building services. Typical lower residential floors contain four to six apartments each. Upper floors contain two to four larger residences per floor, while the top levels hold duplex and full-floor penthouses. Underground and podium parking add approximately 20,000 to 30,000 m² beyond the tower's above-ground floor area.

== History ==

The tower was constructed between 2012 and 2015 by [[Grup Ciutat Nova]], which had previously focused on commercial office development in the [[Districte Financer (Original, Sant Cristòfor)|Districte Financer]]. The project was part of the continued conversion of the former docklands of [[Molls Superiors (Original, Sant Cristòfor)|Molls Superiors]] and [[Molls Inferiors (Original, Sant Cristòfor)|Molls Inferiors]] into high-end residential and commercial use, a process that began in the 1990s.

The tower's height and slender profile made it an immediate landmark on the Sant Cristòfor waterfront. Its completion marked the first time a residential building surpassed the height of the nearby office towers, and it remains the tallest residential tower in the city.

== Use ==

2215 Avinguda Embarcadero operates as a luxury apartment building. The tower houses approximately 280 apartments, ranging from one-bedroom units to large duplex penthouses. Amenities include a residents' lounge, fitness centre, spa, indoor pool, concierge service, and private dining facilities. The building is marketed toward affluent professionals, expatriates, and canal corridor executives.

